================================================================
DBT ON ECS: MIGRATION GUIDE
EC2 to Fargate
================================================================
Version: 1.0 (POC)
Status: Draft

----------------------------------------------------------------
OVERVIEW
----------------------------------------------------------------
This document describes the migration path for tenants moving
their DBT workloads from ECS EC2 to ECS Fargate.

The migration has been designed to minimize tenant effort.
Most infrastructure changes are handled transparently by the
platform team via updated Service Catalog products.

----------------------------------------------------------------
CURRENT STATE (ECS EC2)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Each tenant provisions a Service Catalog product which creates:

  - State Machine (Step Functions)
  - ECS Task IAM Role
  - SM IAM Role
  - ECS Log Group
  - SM Log Group
  - ECS Cluster
  - Auto Scaling Group (launches EC2 instance)
  - KMS Policies
  - Task Definition (SSM)

Tenants trigger DBT runs via Step Functions, which calls
ECS RunTask on the provisioned EC2-backed cluster.

----------------------------------------------------------------
FUTURE STATE (ECS FARGATE)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Each tenant provisions an updated Service Catalog product
which creates:

  - State Machine (Step Functions)
  - ECS Task IAM Role
  - SM IAM Role
  - ECS Log Group
  - SM Log Group
  - KMS Policies
  - Task Definition (SSM) — Fargate compatible
  - Execution Role (pulls ECR image)

REMOVED:
  - ECS Cluster (no longer needed)
  - Auto Scaling Group (no longer needed)
  - EC2 Instance (no longer needed)

ADDED:
  - ECR Sync product dependency (one-time prerequisite)

----------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT CHANGES FOR TENANTS
----------------------------------------------------------------
Minimal impact. Summary of delta:

  1. ECR Sync Product (NEW - one-time action)
     Tenants must run the ECR Sync Service Catalog product
     before migration. This pulls the DBT image from Nexus
     into the local ECR repository.
     This is a one-time step per tenant.

  2. Service Catalog Product (UPDATED)
     Tenants provision the updated Fargate-flavored product
     instead of the EC2 one. The provisioning experience
     is the same.

NOTHING ELSE CHANGES for the tenant.

----------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT DOES NOT CHANGE FOR TENANTS
----------------------------------------------------------------
  - How they trigger DBT runs (Step Functions, same interface)
  - Subnets (already passed as input parameters, unchanged)
  - Security Groups (Border Control SG is attached
    automatically at product provisioning time)
  - IAM role provisioning (handled by platform)
  - Logging setup (same log group structure)
  - KMS policies

----------------------------------------------------------------
PREREQUISITES FOR MIGRATION
----------------------------------------------------------------
Before a tenant can migrate, the following must be in place:

  [ ] ECR Sync Service Catalog product is available
  [ ] Tenant has run the ECR Sync product successfully
      and DBT image is confirmed in local ECR
  [ ] Updated Fargate Service Catalog product is published
      and available in tenant's Service Catalog portfolio
  [ ] Subnets are confirmed and available as input parameters
  [ ] Border Control Security Group is confirmed and will
      be attached at provisioning time

----------------------------------------------------------------
MIGRATION STEPS (PER TENANT)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Step 1 — Run ECR Sync Product
  - Launch the ECR Sync Service Catalog product
  - Provide the Nexus image reference as parameter
  - Confirm DBT image is successfully synced to ECR
  - This is a one-time action

Step 2 — Provision New Fargate Service Catalog Product
  - Deprovision the existing EC2 Service Catalog product
    (or keep running in parallel during validation)
  - Launch the updated Fargate Service Catalog product
  - Input parameters remain the same:
      * TaskDefinitionSSM
      * SyncNexusImage = True
      * Subnets (existing values, no change)
  - Security Group is attached automatically

Step 3 — Validate
  - Trigger a DBT run via Step Functions
  - Confirm Fargate task launches successfully
  - Confirm DBT execution completes
  - Confirm logs are available in ECS Log Group
  - Confirm no errors in State Machine execution

Step 4 — Decommission EC2 Resources (post validation)
  - Deprovision old EC2 Service Catalog product
    if kept running in parallel
  - Confirm ASG and EC2 instance are terminated
  - Confirm no orphaned resources remain

----------------------------------------------------------------
FARGATE TASK RUNTIME BEHAVIOR
----------------------------------------------------------------
When a DBT run is triggered on Fargate:

  1. Step Functions invokes ECS RunTask via SM IAM Role
  2. ECS validates the Task Definition
  3. Fargate provisions isolated compute with:
       - Dedicated ENI (Elastic Network Interface)
       - CPU and memory as defined in task definition
       - Attached to tenant subnets
       - Border Control Security Group applied
  4. Execution Role assumes permissions and pulls
     DBT image from local ECR
  5. DBT execution begins
  6. Task terminates on completion (no persistent instance)

----------------------------------------------------------------
KEY BENEFITS OF FARGATE FOR TENANTS
----------------------------------------------------------------
  - No EC2 instance to manage or patch
  - No Auto Scaling Group configuration
  - Fully isolated compute per DBT run
  - Pay per execution (no idle instance cost)
  - No networking burden on tenant side

----------------------------------------------------------------
KNOWN LIMITATIONS (POC SCOPE)
----------------------------------------------------------------
  - This migration guide is based on POC findings
  - Border Control SG used for POC — production SG
    strategy to be confirmed
  - Full load and performance testing not yet completed
  - Rollback plan: tenants can revert to EC2 product
    if issues are found post migration

----------------------------------------------------------------
ROLLBACK PLAN
----------------------------------------------------------------
If issues are found post migration:

  1. Re-provision the EC2 Service Catalog product
  2. Verify EC2 cluster and ASG are back in place
  3. Trigger a test DBT run on EC2 to confirm
  4. Raise findings with platform team before
     reattempting Fargate migration

----------------------------------------------------------------
SUPPORT
----------------------------------------------------------------
For migration support or questions, contact the platform team.
All infrastructure changes are owned by the platform team.
Tenants are only responsible for Steps 1 and 2 above.

